  "limits": [
    "One continuum-response step, no new population, charge-neutrality, global line closure, thermal or wind solve.",
    "No new He line transfer or He two-photon spectrum; positive two-photon energy forcing is reported separately.",
    "Frequency adequacy requires a paired order comparison; a single refined grid is not sufficient.",
    "Selected continuum pump fields are measured before line attenuation and line-rate coupling; they are not revised final line rates.",
    "Only cells2\u20137 receive the replacement He coefficients; all original lower2 LTE coefficients, ne, H, molecules, metals, HeIII, T, density, flow and boundary are retained.",
    "HeII opacity and its ionic free-free contribution update once in C; its HeIII capture source and native treatment of induced continuum remain unchanged.",
    "The corrected He64 populations were solved in the original background. This is one radiation update, not a converged joint He-continuum fixed point.",
    "No revised He resonance-line transport or two-photon spectrum is inserted. Their positive emitted/absorbed powers are not net additional heating or temperature/error bounds.",
    "Faint hard-UV channels depend on the unchanged explicit zero stellar shortwave tail. A real stellar EUV extension is a separate boundary experiment.",
    "All six full-use requirements remain unknown. No whole-atmosphere/observer/IFT/NUTS or general omitted-He adequacy follows.",
    "Lower-cell coefficients are preserved bitwise between cases within each frequency grid; the radiation arriving at those cells can change.",
